          "code": "DISPLAY_NO_STOCKOUTS_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1776199161617",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776199161619_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate the following confirmation message exactly as written, without adding or modifying any text.\n\nNo stockouts found. Check if the selling price is defined for the items or select a different plan."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CHART",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "display table"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_TABLE",
          "id": "1776287490645",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776287490645_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to generate a Table and a chart using the data from the following variable:\n{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_STOCKOUT_TABLE_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nInstructions:\n- If {{$context.$nodes.CREATE_STOCKOUT_TABLE_DATA.$output.result}} is null, empty, undefined, or contains no rows, display only: No stockouts found.\n\n- Do NOT render:\n  - Table\n  - Chart\n  - Headers\n  - Descriptions\n  - Any additional text\n\nDo not render any currency symbol for any revenue related fields \n\n- Only when data exists, render the table first and the chart immediately below it.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTABLE SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\nHEADER Title Requirement:\n\nGenerate a concise business-friendly header using:\nbusiness entity - {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nplan Name - {{$context.$nodes.TOP_STOCKOUTS_DATA.$output.planName}}\n\nIdentify the business entity type from the user request (Item, Location, Segment, etc.) and include it in the title.\n\nFormat:\nStockout Risk for <EntityType> <EntityValue> for Plan <planName>\n\nDo NOT repeat the exact user query.\nDo NOT include conversational phrases like \"Show me\", \"Display\", or \"Give me\".\n\nExamples:\n- Stockout Risk for Item <Item Name> for Plan <Plan Name>\n- Stockout Risk for Location <Location Name> for Plan < Plan Name>\n\nGenerate the table description dynamically using key business values from the table data. The description should summarize the most critical stockout risks, highest revenue exposure, impacted locations, and earliest stockout timing in a concise business-friendly sentence.\n\nTable Requirements:\nDisplay a table with the following columns only:\n- Segment\n- Item\n- Location\n- Status\n- Revenue at Risk\n- First Stockout Date (Format should be MM-DD-YYYY)\n- First Stockout Quantity\n- First Stockout Value\n\nStatus Column Requirement:\n- Render the Status value as a badge (pill/label style UI element).\n- Apply color coding based on the status value.\n- The status value must always be \"Need Action\" for all rows.\n\nRow Actions:\nFor every row, generate the following action by substituting values from the dataset:\n\nora.Invoke(Review, {\n  \"command\": \"Review\",\n  \"PlanId\": \"{{$context.$nodes.TOP_STOCKOUTS_DATA.$output.planId}}\",\n  \"inventoryItemId\": \"<inventoryItemId>\",\n  \"organizationId\": \"<organizationId>\",\n  \"SegmentName\": \"<Segment>\",\n  \"ItemName\": \"<Item>\",\n  \"Location\": \"<Location>\",\n  \"PlanName\": \"{{$context.$nodes.TOP_STOCKOUTS_DATA.$output.planName}}\"\n})\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCHART SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nGenerate the chart description dynamically by summarizing the comparative revenue exposure across impacted item-location combinations and highlighting which items contribute the highest business risk.\n\nChart Requirements:\n- Type: Bar chart\n- X-axis: \"Item - Location\"\n- Y-axis: Revenue at Risk\n\nStrict Rules:\n- Chart should be rendered large and fully occupy the available container space.\n- Each bar must represent exactly ONE row from the dataset.\n- Do NOT aggregate, group, merge, or summarize data.\n- Even if multiple rows have the same Item, they must appear separately.\n- The number of bars must exactly match the number of rows in the table.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nFinal Constraints:\n- Do not include any HEADER Title section.\n- Do not include subtitles, descriptions, insights, or any extra text beyond what is explicitly requested.\n- Only render the table and chart when valid data exists."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "prepare stockout table data",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const response = $context.$nodes.GET_TOP_STOCKOUT_DATA.$output;\nconst items = $context.$nodes.GET_PLAN_NAME.$output.items || [];\n\n\nif (response && response.stockoutInsights && response.stockoutInsights.length > 0) {\n    \n    const result = response.stockoutInsights\n        .filter(item => [1, 2, 3].includes(item.rank))\n        .map(item => {\n            const firstStockoutValue = item.firstStockoutQty * item.price;\n\n            return {\n              \"Segment\": item.segmentName,\n                \"Item\": item.itemName,\n                \"Location\": item.organizationCode,\n                \"Revenue at Risk\": item.revenueImpact,\n                \"First Stockout Date\": item.firstStockoutDate,\n                \"First Stockout Quantity\": item.firstStockoutQty,\n                \"First Stockout Value\": firstStockoutValue,\n                 \"organizationId\": item.orgLvlMemberId,\n                 \"inventoryItemId\": item.prdLvlMemberId,\n                PlanName: items[0].CompileDesignator,\n            };\n        });\n\n    return result;\n}\n\nreturn [];"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777936667823"
          },
          "code": "PREPARE_STOCKOUT_TABLE_DATA",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776199093730",
          "id": "1775604086159",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CHART"
              ]
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "description": "",
            "name": "Display Top Stockouts"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_TOP_STOCKOUTS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776199093730",
          "id": "1776123097379",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776123097379_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to generate a Table and a chart using the data from the following variable:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_STOCKOUT_TABLE_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nInstructions:\nFollow all instructions strictly. Do not add any extra text, headings, summaries, descriptions, or explanations beyond what is explicitly specified.\nDo not render any currency symbol for any revenue related fields \n\nLayout Requirement:\n- The table MUST be rendered first.\n- The bar chart MUST be rendered immediately below the table.\n- Do not place the chart above the table.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTABLE SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nHEADER Title:\nTop 3 stockout items by revenue for plan {{$context?.$nodes?.PREPARE_STOCKOUT_TABLE_DATA?.$output?.result?.[0]?.PlanName || \"\"}}\nGenerate the table description dynamically using key business values from the table data. The description should summarize the most critical stockout risks, highest revenue exposure, impacted locations, and earliest stockout timing in a concise business-friendly sentence.\n\nTable Requirements:\nDisplay a table with the following columns only:\n- Segment\n- Item\n- Location\n- Status\n- Revenue at Risk\n- First Stockout Date(Format should be MM-DD-YYYY)\n- First Stockout Quantity\n- First Stockout Value\n\nStatus Column Requirement:\n- Render the Status value as a badge (pill/label style UI element).\n- Apply color coding based on the status value.\n- The status value must always be \"Need Action\" for all rows.\n\nRow Actions:\nFor every row, generate the following action by substituting values from the dataset:\n\nora.Invoke(Review, {\n  \"command\": \"Review\",\n  \"PlanId\": \"{{$context.$nodes.GETPLANIDCONTEXT.$output.result}}\",\n  \"inventoryItemId\": \"<inventoryItemId>\",\n  \"organizationId\": \"<organizationId>\",\n   \"SegmentName\":  \"<Segment>\",\n    \"ItemName\":\"<Item>\",\n     \"Location\":\"<Location>\",\n     \"PlanName\":\"{{$context?.$nodes?.PREPARE_STOCKOUT_TABLE_DATA?.$output?.result?.[0]?.PlanName}}\"\n})\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCHART SECTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nHEADER Title:\nRevenue at risk\nGenerate the chart description dynamically by summarizing the comparative revenue exposure across impacted item-location combinations and highlighting which items contribute the highest business risk.\nChart Requirements:\n- Type: Bar chart\n- X-axis: Each row must be represented uniquely using:\n  \"Item - Location\"\n- Y-axis: Revenue at Risk\n\nStrict Rules:\nChart should be rendered large, fully occupying the available container space, and must match the container’s full width and height.\n- Each bar must represent exactly ONE row from the dataset.\n- Do NOT aggregate, group, merge, or summarize data.\n- Even if multiple rows have the same Item, they must appear separately.\n- The number of bars must exactly match the number of rows in the table.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nFinal Constraints:\n- Do not include subtitles, descriptions, insights, or any additional text.\n- Only render the table and the chart with the exact headers specified above."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
