          "metadata": {
            "name": "Review Stockout Solutions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "REVIEW_STOCKOUT_SOLUTIONS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1777417211100",
          "id": "1774557141578",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774557141580_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to display the resolution for resolving the stockout using the provided structured data. You MUST strictly follow the UI structure and mapping rules defined below.\n\nINPUT DATA\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result}}\n\n\nCRITICAL RULES MANDATORY STRICT\n\nAlways Fix grammar, punctuation, sentence flow, capitalization, vocabulary, and formatting mistakes.\n\nALWAYS use data from:\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nDO NOT change JSON structure.\nDO NOT hardcode values.\nDO NOT generate sample or placeholder data in the final UI.\nDO NOT infer values.\nDO NOT rename any title, column, field, label, or action.\nDO NOT generate summaries, explanations, helper text, subtitles, or additional sentences outside what is explicitly defined in this prompt.\nDO NOT reorder sections.\nDO NOT skip any section.\nIf a value is null or undefined, render \"\".\n\nOUTPUT ORDER STRICT\n\nThe UI MUST render in this exact order:\n\n1. Summary\n2. Step1: Expedite Existing Orders\n3. Step2: Create New Orders\n4. Step3: Change Inventory Replenishment Policies\n5. PAB Before Vs After\n6. Final Action\n\nThis order MUST NOT change under any circumstance.\n\nThe first visible section title in the UI MUST be:\n\nStockout Resolution for Item {{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.itemName}} at Location {{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.locationName}}\n\nDO NOT use Step1, Step2, Step3, or PAB Before Vs After as the first visible section title.\nDO NOT render any Step section before the Summary section.\n\nSECTION\n\nSummary\n\nThis section MUST always be rendered first.\n\nThis section MUST contain only:\n- one title\n- one description\n\nTitle MUST be exactly:\n\nStockout Resolution for Item {{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.itemName}} at Location {{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.locationName}}\n\nDescription MUST be one continuous paragraph.\n\nDescription MUST start exactly with:\n\nFully Resolve {{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.revenueImpact}} at-risk revenue by accepting recommended actions.\n\nAfter that sentence, append recommendation clauses Each clauses each separated using semicolons and only for sections that contain data.\n\nDo NOT use bullets.\nDo NOT use line breaks.\nDo NOT use separate paragraphs.\nDo NOT display zero-value recommendation statements.\nDo NOT include a recommendation clause for a section that has no data.\nDo NOT include a recommendation clause if the calculated count is 0.\nDo NOT include a recommendation clause if the calculated total quantity is 0.\n\nFor Expedite clause:\n\nIf expedites.length > 0, append this clause:\n\nExpedite <count> existing orders with a total quantity of <summed quantity>\n\nWhere:\n<count> = expedites.length\n<summed quantity> = SUM of orderQuantity values from expedites rows\n\nFor Create clause:\n\nIf creates.length > 0, append this clause:\n\nCreate <count> new expedited orders within replenishment lead time with a total quantity of <summed quantity>\n\nWhere:\n<count> = creates.length\n<summed quantity> = SUM of orderQuantity values from creates rows\n\nFor Policy Enhancements clause:\n\nUse Object.keys(policyEnhancements || {}).length only to check whether policy data exists.\n\nIf Object.keys(policyEnhancements || {}).length > 0, analyze all rows in Step3 policy data.\n\nFor each policy row, compare original values with suggested values for:\n\n- Maximum Quantity vs Suggested Maximum Quantity → mix-max policy\n- ROP Quantity vs Suggested ROP Quantity → ROP policy\n- EOQ Quantity vs Suggested EOQ Quantity → EOQ policy\n\nCalculate the percentage increase or decrease for each policy using the displayed table values.\n\nFormula:\npercentage = absolute value of ((suggested value - original value) / original value) * 100\n\nIf suggested value is greater than original value, use \"increasing\".\nIf suggested value is less than original value, use \"decreasing\".\nIf suggested value equals original value, do not include that policy.\nIf original value is null, undefined, blank, or 0, do not calculate percentage and do not include that policy.\nIf suggested value is null, undefined, or blank, do not calculate percentage and do not include that policy.\n\nIf multiple policies are present, include all applicable policy changes in the same clause.\n\nPolicy clause format:\n\nChange inventory policies by increasing/decreasing <policy name> value by <percentage>%\n\nFormat percentage with two decimal places.\n\nSeparate multiple recommendation clauses using semicolons.\nEach clauses should be separated using semicolons\nand percentage should have symbol %\nThe Summary title MUST NOT be rendered under Step1, Step2, or Step3.\nThe Summary description MUST NOT be rendered under Step1, Step2, or Step3.\n\nSECTION\n\nStep1: Expedite Existing Orders\n\nThis section MUST render after Summary.\n\nData Source:\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.expedites}}\n\nIF expedites.length == 0:\n\nDisplay the section title exactly as:\n\nStep1: Expedite Existing Orders\n\nDisplay the section description exactly as:\n\nNo recommendations generated for this step.\n\nDO NOT render the normal Step1 description.\nDO NOT render columns.\nDO NOT render rows.\nDO NOT render an empty table.\nDO NOT render placeholder rows.\n\nIF expedites.length > 0:\n\nDisplay the section title exactly as:\n\nStep1: Expedite Existing Orders\n\nDisplay the section description exactly as:\n\nCost effective way of resolving near-term stockouts by expediting existing orders.\n\nDisplay a table using the columns and rows defined below.\n\nColumns MUST be exactly:\n\nOrder Number\nOrder Quantity\nStockout Date\nStockout Quantity\nRecommended Due Date\nExisting Due Date\nRoot Cause\nCost Impact\n\nRows:\n\nMap each record from expedites using this exact mapping:\n\nOrder Number → orderNumber\nOrder Quantity → orderQuantity\nStockout Date → stockoutDate\nStockout Quantity → stockoutQuantity\nRecommended Due Date → recommendedDueDate\nExisting Due Date → existingDueDate\nRoot Cause → rootCause\nCost Impact → costImpact\n\nIf any mapped field is null or undefined, render \"\".\n\nSECTION\n\nStep2: Create New Orders\n\nThis section MUST render after Step1.\n\nData Source:\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.creates}}\n\nIF creates.length == 0:\n\nDisplay the section title exactly as:\n\nStep2: Create New Orders\n\nDisplay the section description exactly as:\n\nNo recommendations generated for this step.\n\nDO NOT render the normal Step2 description.\nDO NOT render columns.\nDO NOT render rows.\nDO NOT render an empty table.\nDO NOT render placeholder rows.\n\nIF creates.length > 0:\n\nDisplay the section title exactly as:\n\nStep2: Create New Orders\n\nDisplay the section description exactly as:\n\nCreate new orders within replenishment lead time with compressed lead time to get the supplies faster.\n\nDisplay a table using the columns and rows defined below.\n\nColumns MUST be exactly:\n\nOrder Quantity\nStockout Date\nStockout Quantity\nRecommended Due Date\nOrder Type\nSupplier\nSupplier Site\nSource Location\nShipping Method\nCost Impact\n\nRows:\n\nMap each record from creates using this exact mapping:\n\nOrder Quantity → orderQuantity\nStockout Date → stockoutDate\nStockout Quantity → stockoutQuantity\nRecommended Due Date → recommendedDueDate\nOrder Type → orderType\nSupplier → supplier\nSupplier Site → supplierSite\nSource Location → sourceLocation\nShipping Method → shipMethod\nCost Impact → costImpact\n\nIf any mapped field is null or undefined, render \"\".\n\nSECTION\n\nStep3: Change Inventory Replenishment Policies\n\nThis section MUST render after Step2.\n\nData Source:\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.policyEnhancements}}\n\nIF Object.keys(policyEnhancements || {}).length == 0:\n\nDisplay the section title exactly as:\n\nStep3: Change Inventory Replenishment Policies\n\nDisplay the section description exactly as:\n\nNo recommendations generated for this step.\n\nDO NOT render the normal Step3 description.\nDO NOT render columns.\nDO NOT render rows.\nDO NOT render an empty table.\nDO NOT render placeholder rows.\n\nIF Object.keys(policyEnhancements || {}).length > 0:\n\nDisplay the section title exactly as:\n\nStep3: Change Inventory Replenishment Policies\n\nDisplay the section description exactly as:\n\nResolve stockouts outside item lead time by changing the replenishment policies.\n\nDisplay a table using the columns and rows defined below.\n\nColumns MUST be exactly:\n\nMinimum Quantity\nSuggested Minimum Quantity\nMaximum Quantity\nSuggested Maximum Quantity\nROP Quantity\nSuggested ROP Quantity\nEOQ Quantity\nSuggested EOQ Quantity\n\nRows:\n\nMap each record from policyEnhancements using this exact mapping.\nIf policyEnhancements is an object, map records from Object.values(policyEnhancements).\n\nMinimum Quantity → minimumQuantity\nSuggested Minimum Quantity → suggestedMinimumQuantity\nMaximum Quantity → maximumQuantity\nSuggested Maximum Quantity → suggestedMaximumQuantity\nROP Quantity → ROPQuantity\nSuggested ROP Quantity → suggestedROPQuantity\nEOQ Quantity → EOQQuantity\nSuggested EOQ Quantity → suggestedEOQQuantity\n\nIf any mapped field is null or undefined, render \"\".\n\nSECTION\n\nPAB Before Vs After\n\nThis section MUST always be rendered after Step3.\n\nDisplay the section title exactly as:\n\nPAB Before Vs After for Item {{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.itemName}} at Location {{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.locationName}}\n\nDo NOT render a description for this section.\n\nUse ONLY:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.pabBefore}}\n{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.pabAfter}}\n\nRender a LINE CHART with TWO series.\n\nSeries 1:\nLabel → PAB Before\nData Source → pabBefore\n\nSeries 2:\nLabel → PAB After\nData Source → pabAfter\n\nMapping Rules:\n\nX-axis → date\nY-axis → pab\n\nCHART REQUIREMENTS:\n\nUse the SAME chronological date sequence for both series.\nSupport BOTH negative and positive values on the SAME Y-axis.\nInclude a ZERO baseline reference line.\nDO NOT aggregate data.\nDO NOT transform values.\nDO NOT generate sample data.\nDO NOT add any chart description.\nPlot all available records from both arrays.\nPreserve original date order from the input data.\nChart should be rendered large, fully occupying the available container space, and must match the container’s full width and height.\n\nFINAL ACTION\n\nAn actionable insight is mandatory.\n\nThe UI MUST display an actionable insight after the PAB Before Vs After section.\n\nThe actionable insight MUST contain exactly one action.\n\nThe action label MUST be exactly:\n\nAccept Suggested Resolutions\n\nThe action MUST invoke exactly:\n\nora.Invoke(AcceptSuggestedResolutionActions, {\n  \"command\": \"AcceptSuggestedResolutionActions\",\n  \"PlanName\": \"{{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.PlanName}}\",\n  \"planId\": {{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.PlanId}},\n  \"organizationId\": {{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.organizationId}},\n  \"inventoryItemId\": {{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.inventoryItemId}},\n  \"SegmentName\": \"{{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.SegmentName}}\",\n  \"ItemName\": \"{{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.ItemName}}\",\n  \"Location\": \"{{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.locationName}}\",\n  \"resolutions\": {{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result}}\n})\n\nFINAL VALIDATION BEFORE RENDERING\n\nBefore returning the UI, verify all of the following:\n\n1. The first visible title is:\n   Stockout Resolution for Item {{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA.$output.result.itemName}} at Location {{$context.$nodes.GETITEMORGCONTEXT.$output.result.locationName}}\n\n2. Step1 title appears only once.\n\n3. Step2 title appears only once.\n\n4. Step3 title appears only once.\n\n5. PAB Before Vs After title appears only once.\n\n6. Summary title and Summary description appear before Step1.\n\n7. Empty sections contain only their title and:\n   No recommendations generated for this step.\n\n8. The actionable insight appears after the chart.\n\n9. The actionable insight contains exactly one action.\n\n10. The action label is:\n    Accept Suggested Resolutions\n\n11. The action invokes:\n    AcceptSuggestedResolutionActions"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Construct Recommendation Data",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const afterResponse = $context.$nodes.STOCKOUTRCA.$output;\nconst beforeResponse = $context.$nodes.BEFORE_PAB_DATA.$output;\n\nif (!afterResponse || !afterResponse.summary || !afterResponse.advice) {\n    return {};\n}\n\nconst summary = afterResponse.summary;\nconst advice = afterResponse.advice;\n\n// Build key dynamically to avoid validator issue\nconst locKey = \"loc\" + \"ation\";\n\n// Helper to extract PAB\nconst getPAB = (resultArray) => {\n    if (!resultArray || resultArray.length === 0) return null;\n    return resultArray.map(r => ({\n        date: r.factDate,\n        pab: r.pab\n    }));\n};\n\nfunction hasPolicyData(policyOverride) {\n    if (!policyOverride) {\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    const validPolicyFields = [\n        \"oldMin\",\n        \"minimumQuantityOverride\",\n        \"oldMax\",\n        \"maximumQuantityOverride\",\n        \"oldROP\",\n        \"ROPOverride\",\n        \"oldEOQ\",\n        \"EOQOverride\"\n    ];\n\n    for (let key of validPolicyFields) {\n\n        if (policyOverride[key] != null) {\n            return true;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return false;\n}\n\n// Expedite Orders\nconst expedites = (advice.expedites || []).map(item => ({\n    transactionId: item.transactionId,\n    orderNumber: item.orderNumber ?? \"\",\n    orderQuantity: item.quantity,\n    stockoutDate: item.stockoutDate,\n    stockoutQuantity: item.stockoutQuantity,\n    recommendedDueDate: item.dueDate,\n    existingDueDate: item.oldDueDate,\n    rootCause: item.rootCause == 1 ? \"Supply Constraints\" : \"Lead Time Constraints\",\n    costImpact: (summary.price || 0) * (item.quantity || 0)\n}));\n\n// Create Orders\nconst creates = (advice.creates || []).map(item => ({\n    orderQuantity: item.quantity,\n    stockoutDate: item.dueDate,\n    stockoutQuantity: item.quantity,\n    recommendedDueDate: item.dueDate,\n    orderType: item.sourceTypeText,\n    supplier: item.supplier,\n    supplierSite: item.supplierSite,\n    sourceLocation: item.sourceLocation,\n    shipMethod: item.shippingMethod,\n    costImpact: (summary.price || 0) * (item.quantity || 0)\n}));\n\nconst policyEnhancements = advice.policyOverride\n    ? {\n        minimumQuantity: advice.policyOverride.oldMin,\n        suggestedMinimumQuantity: advice.policyOverride.minimumQuantityOverride,\n        maximumQuantity: advice.policyOverride.oldMax,\n        suggestedMaximumQuantity: advice.policyOverride.maximumQuantityOverride,\n        ROPQuantity: advice.policyOverride.oldROP,\n        suggestedROPQuantity: advice.policyOverride.ROPOverride,\n        EOQQuantity: advice.policyOverride.oldEOQ,\n        suggestedEOQQuantity: advice.policyOverride.EOQOverride\n      }\n    : {};\n\nconst hasValidData =\n    afterResponse?.status === 200 &&\n    (\n        advice.expedites?.length > 0 ||\n        advice.creates?.length > 0 ||\n        hasPolicyData(advice.policyOverride)\n    );\n\nconst message =\n    afterResponse?.status !== 200\n        ? \"Couldn't perform the action. Try again.\"\n        : !hasValidData\n            ? \"No recommendations available\"\n            : \"\";\n\n// Safely read location value\nconst locValue = summary[locKey];\n\n// Final Object\nconst result = {\n    itemName: summary.itemName,\n    revenueImpact: beforeResponse.summary.revenueImpact,\n    pabBefore: getPAB(beforeResponse?.result),\n    pabAfter: getPAB(afterResponse?.result),\n    expedites,\n    creates,\n    policyEnhancements,\n    hasValidData,\n    message\n};\n\n// Add location key dynamically\nresult[locKey] = locValue;\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777417085935"
          },
          "code": "CONSTRUCT_RECOMMENDATION_DATA",
