          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CHART",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Table and graph"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_TABLE_AND_GRAPH",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1779389102593",
          "id": "1777251346433",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777251346435_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to display the resolution for resolving the stockout using the provided structured data. You MUST strictly follow the UI structure and mapping rules defined below.\n\nINPUT DATA\n\n{{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_TABLE_DATA.$output.result}}\n\nYou are given structured JSON data. You MUST generate UI only from the input below.\n\n\nCRITICAL RULES (MANDATORY - STRICT)\nALWAYS use the input data\nAlways Fix grammar, punctuation, sentence flow, capitalization, vocabulary, and formatting mistakes.\nDO NOT hardcode values\nDO NOT generate sample or placeholder data\nDO NOT generate summaries, explanations, or additional text\nDO NOT generate extra titles, subtitles, or descriptions\nDO NOT generate any additional explanatory sentence under section titles\nUSE ONLY the exact headings, labels, and text defined in this prompt\nDO NOT rename or modify any heading or column name\nDO NOT skip any section except when the section is explicitly empty\nDo not render currency symbol for revenue fields \nIf arrays contain data → render rows\nIf a field is missing → use \"\"\nNEVER render empty tables\nNEVER render placeholder rows\n\nANY VIOLATION OF THESE RULES IS NOT ALLOWED\n\nRENDERING INSTRUCTION (MANDATORY)\n\nDO NOT reorder sections\n\nSECTION\n\nThis section MUST always be rendered and Do Not use cardwidget\n\nTitle:\n\nStockout Resolution for Item {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.itemName}} at Location {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.locationName}}\n\nDescription must be:\n\nResolve {{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_TABLE_DATA.$output.result.revenueImpact}} at-risk revenue by accepting the recommended actions.\n\nRender the recommendation summary as ONE continuous paragraph.\n\nDo NOT use bullets, line breaks, or separate paragraphs.\n\nOnly include recommendation clauses for sections that contain data.\n\nIf a section has no data, omit that clause entirely.\n\nDo NOT display zero-value recommendation statements.\n\nFor Expedite and Create:\n\nTotal quantity must be calculated as the SUM of \"Order Quantity\" values from the displayed table rows.\n\nFor Policy Enhancements:\n\nUse Object.keys(advice.policyOverride || {}).length only to check whether policy data exists.\nAnalyze all rows in the Step policy table.\nFor each policy row, compare original values with suggested values for:\nMaximum Quantity vs Suggested Maximum Quantity → mix-max policy\nROP Quantity vs Suggested ROP Quantity → ROP policy\nEOQ Quantity vs Suggested EOQ Quantity → EOQ policy\nCalculate the percentage increase or decrease for each policy using displayed table values.\nIf multiple policies are present, include all applicable policy changes in the same clause.\n\nAppend recommendation clauses continuously in this format:\n\nExpedite <count> existing orders with a total quantity of <summed quantity>.\nCreate <count> new expedited orders within replenishment lead time with a total quantity of <summed quantity>.\nChange inventory policies by increasing/decreasing <policy name> value by <percentage>%.\n\nSeparate multiple clauses using semicolons.\nEach clauses should be separated using semicolons\nand percentage should have symbol %\n\nExample Output:\n\nResolve 2.3M at-risk revenue by accepting recommended actions. Expedite 2 existing orders with a total quantity of 96; Create 2 new expedited orders within replenishment lead time with a total quantity of 200; Change inventory policies by increasing mix-max policy value by 21.04% and increasing ROP policy value by 15.00%.\n\nSECTION\n\nRENDER THIS ENTIRE SECTION ONLY IF advice.expedites.length > 0\n\nIf advice.expedites.length == 0:\n\nDO NOT render the section\nDO NOT render title\nDO NOT render description\nDO NOT render table\nDO NOT render any message\n\nTitle: Expedite Existing Orders\n\nDescription:\nCost effective way of resolving near-term stockouts by expediting existing orders.\n\nMULTI RECORD Columns (EXACT):\n\nOrder Number → orderNumber\nOrder Quantity → orderQuantity\nStockout Date → stockoutDate\nStockout Quantity → stockoutQuantity\nRecommended Due Date → recommendedDueDate\nExisting Due Date → existingDueDate\nRoot Cause → rootCause\nCost Impact → costImpact\n\nRows:\nMap each object from advice.expedites array\n\nSECTION\n\nRENDER THIS ENTIRE SECTION ONLY IF advice.creates.length > 0\n\nIf advice.creates.length == 0:\n\nDO NOT render the section\nDO NOT render title\nDO NOT render description\nDO NOT render table\nDO NOT render any message\n\nTitle: Create New Orders\n\nDescription:\nCreate new orders within replenishment lead time with compressed lead time to get the supplies faster.\n\nMULTI RECORD Columns (EXACT):\n\nOrder Quantity → orderQuantity\nStockout Date → stockoutDate\nStockout Quantity → stockoutQuantity\nRecommended Due Date → recommendedDueDate\nOrder Type → orderType\nSupplier → supplier\nSupplier Site → supplierSite\nSource Location → sourceLocation\nShipping Method → shipMethod\nCost Impact → costImpact\n\nRows:\nMap each object from advice.creates array\n\nSECTION\n\nRENDER THIS ENTIRE SECTION ONLY IF advice.policyOverride.length > 0\n\nIf advice.policyOverride.length == 0:\n\nDO NOT render the section\nDO NOT render title\nDO NOT render description\nDO NOT render table\nDO NOT render any message\n\nTitle: Change Inventory Replenishment Policies\n\nDescription:\nResolve stockouts outside item lead time by changing the replenishment policies.\n\nMULTI RECORD Columns (EXACT):\n\nMinimum Quantity → minimumQuantity\nSuggested Minimum Quantity → suggestedMinimumQuantity\nMaximum Quantity → maximumQuantity\nSuggested Maximum Quantity → suggestedMaximumQuantity\nROP Quantity → ROPQuantity\nSuggested ROP Quantity → suggestedROPQuantity\nEOQ Quantity → EOQQuantity\nSuggested EOQ Quantity → suggestedEOQQuantity\n\nRows:\nMap each object from advice.policyOverride array\n\nSECTION\n\nTitle:\nPAB Before Vs After for Item {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.itemName}} at Location {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.locationName}}\n\nCHART (LINE GRAPH)\n\nX-axis → dates\nLine 1 → beforePab (label: PAB Before)\nLine 2 → afterPab (label: PAB After)\n\nRules:\n\nUse ONLY dates, beforePab, and afterPab\nDO NOT generate sample data\nDO NOT add any chart description\nChart should be rendered large, fully occupying the available container space, and must match the container’s full width and height.\nFINAL ACTION\n\ngenerate actionable insight. The action button is mandatory and must always be displayed on the UI.\n\nLabel:\nAccept Suggested Resolutions\n\nAction:\nora.Invoke(AcceptSuggestedResolutionActions, {\n\"command\": \"AcceptSuggestedResolutionActions\",\n\"PlanName\": {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.planName}},\n\"planId\": {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.PlanId}},\n\"organizationId\": {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.organizationId}},\n\"inventoryItemId\": {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.inventoryItemId}},\n\"SegmentName\": {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.segmentName}},\n\"ItemName\": {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.itemName}},\n\"Location\": {{$context.$nodes.RECONSTRUCT_DB_DATA.$output.result.locationName}},\n\"resolutions\": {{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_TABLE_DATA.$output.result.resolutions}}\n})"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display No recommendations"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_NO_RECOMMENDATIONS",
          "id": "1779389138272",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779389138273_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate the following confirmation message exactly as written, without adding or modifying any text.\n\nNo recommendations available."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Analyse Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776232314105"
          },
          "code": "ANALYSE_INTENT",
          "id": "1779391477267",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779391477268_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intelligent intent router.\n\nThe user's query is:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTASK\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nClassify the query into exactly ONE intent AND, only for STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS, extract structured filters.\n\nReturn JSON only. No extra text.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINTENTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS\n- STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION\n- OUTOFCONTEXT\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nIMPORTANT ROUTING PRINCIPLES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nApply the rules in this order:\n\n1. First check PRIORITY OVERRIDE RULES.\n2. Then check STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS.\n3. Then check STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION.\n4. Only return OUTOFCONTEXT if none of the above rules match.\n\nClassify based on meaning and domain relevance, not only exact keyword matching.\n\nIgnore casing, punctuation, and surrounding quotes.\n\nFor example, treat these as equivalent:\n- create order\n- create orders\n- create order option\n- create orders option\n- creating new orders\n- new order creation\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nPRIORITY OVERRIDE RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nA) KNOWN STOCKOUT RESOLUTION OPTION OVERRIDE\n\nIf the query contains, refers to, selects, excludes, filters, hides, shows, or mentions any known stockout resolution option, classify as:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION\"\n}\n\nKnown stockout resolution options include semantic matches for:\n\n- create order\n- create orders\n- create new order\n- create new orders\n- order creation\n- new order creation\n- expedite order\n- expedite orders\n- expedite supply\n- policy override\n- policy overrides\n- policy enhancement\n- policy enhancements\n- inventory policy\n- inventory policies\n- minimum quantity\n- maximum quantity\n- ROP quantity\n- EOQ quantity\n- supplier\n- shipping method\n- resolution option\n- resolution options\n- stockout action\n- stockout actions\n- stockout step\n- stockout steps\n\nThis rule applies even if the query is phrased like a UI label, menu item, button label, filter instruction, dropdown option, or selection command.\n\nExamples that MUST be classified as STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION:\n\n- \"SELECT ALL BUT CREATE ORDERS OPTION\"\n- \"select all except create orders\"\n- \"hide create orders option\"\n- \"show create orders option\"\n- \"filter by create orders\"\n- \"choose expedite orders\"\n- \"remove expedite orders option\"\n- \"policy override option\"\n- \"stockout resolution options\"\n- \"resolution steps\"\n- \"order creation action\"\n\nDo NOT classify these as OUTOFCONTEXT only because the word \"stockout\" is missing.\n\nB) FIELD-BASED OVERRIDE RULE\n\nIf the query mentions ANY order-related or policy-related field, or a synonym of these fields, classify as:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION\"\n}\n\nOrder-related fields:\n- Order Number\n- Order Quantity\n- Stockout Date\n- Stockout Quantity\n- Recommended Due Date\n- Existing Due Date\n- Root Cause\n- Cost Impact\n\nPolicy-related fields:\n- Minimum Quantity\n- Maximum Quantity\n- ROP Quantity\n- EOQ Quantity\n- Supplier\n- Shipping Method\n\nExamples:\n\n- \"orders with stockout date 2030-01-06\"\n- \"show orders with quantity > 50\"\n- \"filter by supplier M2\"\n- \"minimum quantity is greater than 100\"\n- \"shipping method is air\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCORE INTENT DEFINITIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1) STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS\n\nUse this when:\n- The user wants to VIEW, LIST, ANALYZE, SHOW, or INSPECT stockouts\nAND\n- The query contains at least one stockout dimension, explicit or implicit\nAND\n- The query does NOT refer to order actions, resolution options, recommendations, or policy fields.\n\nValid dimensions:\n\nA) Explicit keywords:\n- item\n- location\n- plan\n- segment\n\nB) Implicit values:\n- Item identifiers, for example ABC, SKU123\n- Location names or codes, for example DC1, RDC1\n- Plan names, for example PlanA\n- Segment names, for example HighCost\n\nExamples:\n- \"Show stockouts for item ABC and location DC1\"\n- \"Stockouts for ABC in DC1\"\n- \"List stockouts for RDC1\"\n- \"PlanA shortages\"\n- \"HighCost segment stockouts\"\n- \"Top 10 stockouts for item ABC\"\n\nImportant:\n- STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS must include at least one stockout dimension.\n- If the query refers to orders, order creation, expedite orders, recommendations, resolution options, or policy fields, do NOT classify as STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS.\n- In that case, classify as STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n2) STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION\n\nUse this when:\n- The user wants to FIX, RESOLVE, REDUCE, MITIGATE, or ACT on stockouts\nOR\n- The query involves orders, recommendations, creating new orders, expedite orders, inventory policies, policy overrides, or stockout resolution actions\nOR\n- The query refers to any stockout resolution step, option, action, menu item, button, dropdown, or filter\nOR\n- The query semantically implies stockout resolution, even if exact keywords are not present\nOR\n- The query mentions a known resolution option such as create orders, expedite orders, or policy override\n\nExamples:\n- \"Resolve stockouts\"\n- \"Fix stockouts for item ABC\"\n- \"Create orders\"\n- \"Create orders option\"\n- \"SELECT ALL BUT CREATE ORDERS OPTION\"\n- \"Expedite orders\"\n- \"Show recommendations\"\n- \"Apply policy override\"\n- \"Change inventory policy\"\n- \"Filter stockout resolution options\"\n- \"Show resolution steps\"\n- \"Order actions\"\n- \"Recommended actions\"\n\nImportant:\n- Classify by meaning, not only exact keyword matching.\n- A query can be STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION even if it does not contain the word \"stockout\".\n- UI/menu/filter phrases that reference known resolution actions must be STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION.\n- Do not classify a known resolution option as OUTOFCONTEXT just because the query is short or written like a UI command.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n3) OUTOFCONTEXT\n\nUse this only when:\n- The query is clearly unrelated to stockouts, orders, recommendations, inventory policies, or stockout resolution actions\nOR\n- The query is unclear and does not contain any stockout analysis dimension, known resolution option, order-related concept, recommendation-related concept, or policy-related concept.\n\nExamples:\n- \"What is the weather today?\"\n- \"Tell me a joke\"\n- \"Open the dashboard\"\n- \"Change the color\"\n- \"Hello\"\n\nImportant:\n- OUTOFCONTEXT is the fallback intent.\n- Before returning OUTOFCONTEXT, first check whether the query contains a known stockout resolution option such as create orders, expedite orders, or policy override.\n- If it does, return STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCONFLICT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1. If the query matches a PRIORITY OVERRIDE RULE, use that intent first.\n2. If the query contains both a stockout dimension and order/policy/resolution fields, classify as STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION.\n3. If the query contains a stockout dimension and analysis/view/list intent, classify as STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS.\n4. If the query has no dimension but contains action, order, recommendation, resolution, or policy meaning, classify as STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION.\n5. Else classify as OUTOFCONTEXT.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nENTITY EXTRACTION ONLY FOR STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf intent = STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS, extract filters into this exact structure:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS\",\n  \"intents\": [\n    {\n      \"request\": {\n        \"item\": <string or null>,\n        \"location\": <string or null>,\n        \"segment\": <string or null>,\n        \"topN\": <number>\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nField mapping rules:\n- item OR itemName -> item\n- location OR locationName OR organisation OR organization OR organisationName OR organizationName -> location\n- segment OR segmentName -> segment\n\nExtraction rules:\n- If value is not present, return null.\n- Extract exact values only.\n- Do not infer missing values.\n- If \"top N\" is mentioned, extract the number.\n- Example: \"top 10\" -> 10\n- Otherwise default topN to 3.\n- Use key name exactly: \"location\", not \"locationName\".\n- Always include intents[0].request.\n- Always include all fields: item, location, segment, topN.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIF intent = STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS, return:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS\",\n  \"intents\": [\n    {\n      \"request\": {\n        \"item\": \"...\",\n        \"location\": \"...\",\n        \"segment\": \"...\",\n        \"topN\": 3\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nUse null for missing values:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS\",\n  \"intents\": [\n    {\n      \"request\": {\n        \"item\": null,\n        \"location\": \"DC1\",\n        \"segment\": null,\n        \"topN\": 3\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nIF intent = STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION, return:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION\"\n}\n\nIF intent = OUTOFCONTEXT, return:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"OUTOFCONTEXT\"\n}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nFINAL CHECK BEFORE RESPONDING\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore returning JSON, verify:\n\n- Does the query mention or semantically refer to create orders, expedite orders, policy override, inventory policy, recommendations, resolution options, or stockout actions?\n  - If yes, return STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION.\n\n- Does the query ask to view/list/analyze stockouts with item/location/plan/segment?\n  - If yes, return STOCKOUT_ANALYSIS.\n\n- Otherwise return OUTOFCONTEXT.\n\nFor the query \"SELECT ALL BUT CREATE ORDERS OPTION\", return:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"STOCKOUT_RESOLUTION\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
